Subject: [PATCH] vsock/virtio: don't send a credit update after every read

virtio_transport_stream_do_dequeue() sends a credit update when the
receive queue holds fewer bytes than SO_RCVLOWAT. With the default of 1,
that is true whenever a read empties the queue, so a request/response
exchange sent one credit update per message. Each one is a transmit
packet, a queue kick and a completion interrupt: on microvm, 3 of the ~8
VM exits of a vsock round trip.

The free_space test already sends an update before the sender can run
out of credit, so keep the rcvlowat test only for SO_RCVLOWAT > 1, which
is what it was added for.

--- a/net/vmw_vsock/virtio_transport_common.c	2026-11-04 17:59:45.582113527 +0100
+++ b/net/vmw_vsock/virtio_transport_common.c	2026-11-04 17:59:45.674550904 +0100
@@ -770,8 +770,13 @@
 
 	fwd_cnt_delta = vvs->fwd_cnt - vvs->last_fwd_cnt;
 	free_space = vvs->buf_alloc - fwd_cnt_delta;
-	low_rx_bytes = (vvs->rx_bytes <
-			sock_rcvlowat(sk_vsock(vsk), 0, INT_MAX));
+	/* With the default SO_RCVLOWAT of 1, an emptied queue counts as
+	 * "low" after every read, so every read sent a credit update: a
+	 * packet, a kick and an interrupt per message. A sender stalled for
+	 * credit is already caught by the free_space test below.
+	 */
+	low_rx_bytes = sk_vsock(vsk)->sk_rcvlowat > 1 &&
+		       vvs->rx_bytes < sock_rcvlowat(sk_vsock(vsk), 0, INT_MAX);
 
 	spin_unlock_bh(&vvs->rx_lock);
 
